# Pairs with SagaCompletes. Reproduces production before #4475 was fixed (#4531,
# #4581): a saga bound to the
# old copy keeps sending its terminals there, and once the purge has cleared
# that copy and unregistered it, AppendTxTerminalAsync (a non-write that does
# not answer a purged tree as empty) refuses with InvalidOperationException.
# MarkOneShardAsync follows only stale-routing refusals, so the broadcast fails
# on every retry and the saga never completes; the resized copy's mirrored
# buckets stay unresolved behind it.
#
# A second edit lets the stalled saga count as quiescent, so the mutant cannot
# deadlock and the temporal property is the only thing TLC can report.
MODULE: SagaCompletesPurgedCopyRefusesTerminal
TARGET: SagaCompletes
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a saga bound to a purged old copy can never deliver its terminals
PERTURBS: SagaTerminal

--- FIND
    /\ s \in TermTargets \ told
    /\ told' = told \cup {s}
--- REPLACE
    /\ s \in TermTargets \ told
\* MUTATION: the purged old copy refuses the terminal outright.
    /\ ~Gone(bound)
    /\ told' = told \cup {s}
--- END

--- FIND
Quiescent ==
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
--- REPLACE
Quiescent ==
\* MUTATION: a saga stalled on a purged copy is not in flight.
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"} \/ Gone(bound)
--- END
